WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.734
-Welcome back. We're here with
Stephen A. Smith right here.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:08.133
Now, Stephen, we love you.

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.501
You're known
for your strong opinions

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.200
about all kinds
of different topics.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.167
So with that in mind, it's time
to play a game we call

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:14.434
Wheel of Opinions.

00:00:14.434 --> 00:00:15.534
Here we go.
-Let's do it.

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:18.868
-♪ Wheel of Opinions ♪

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:21.367
-Now here's how it works.
I'm going to hit this button

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.534
here, which activates
the opinion topic generator,

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.200
and it will land
on a random topic.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.133
Whatever it is, you have
to give an opinion on it.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.601
-Do I hit the button
or do you hit the button?

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:29.934
-I'll hit the button so you
don't have to worry about that.

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.267
-Alright. Okay.
I appreciate that.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.501
-I don't want you to have to
worry about this stuff.

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:33.701
You're a guest on the show,
come on.

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:34.968
-I appreciate that, man.
That's first class.

00:00:34.968 --> 00:00:36.033
-Yeah, of course.
-That's first class right there.

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.033
Here we go.

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:39.767
♪♪

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:42.067
-Ooh.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.767
-How about fans
who paint their chests?

00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:45.934
-Oh, Lord.

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.167
-What's your thoughts?

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:50.767
-Something's wrong
with those people.

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:52.434
Now, I want to say this.

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:54.467
I want to say this.
It's wrong with them,

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:57.767
but in certain college -- like,
festive college atmosphere,

00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:00.567
those big time football games,
the basketball games,

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:02.133
the tailgate parties
that precede it --

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:03.767
alright, that's fine.

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:07.901
However, however, I don't know
what's wrong with these people

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.167
who do that in cold weather.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:13.267
Like you're in Ohio,
at Ohio State.

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:15.067
Yeah.
-And it's 5 degrees

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.300
and you out there half-naked.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.234
You're at Michigan, Ann Arbor,
half naked.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:22.334
Now, if you did that in
Pasadena,

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:23.734
okay, I'll let you.
-Okay.

00:01:23.734 --> 00:01:26.067
-But when you do that
in the cold weather,

00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:28.567
let me --
let me put to you this way.

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:29.701
Ain't no Black people
doing that.

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:30.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:31.868
Ain't no Black people
doing that.

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.767
We ain't doing that cold stuff.

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:36.067
-Okay. Yeah, okay. Gotcha.
That's good. Okay.

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.400
Let's get to the next topic

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:42.067
♪♪

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:45.868
-Oh!
-Gatorade showers.

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:48.601
-Very nasty.

00:01:48.601 --> 00:01:49.667
Now, don't get me wrong --

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:52.234
if you need your electrolytes,
it works.

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:53.467
It works.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.434
But, you know --

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.801
and it don't matter when you win

00:01:57.801 --> 00:01:59.801
because it don't matter --
I mean, listen,

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:02.067
most people,
if you notice, when they win it,

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.934
whether it's the champagne
or it's the water or whatever,

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:06.901
is coming with funk.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:08.868
They're going to
stink afterwards, okay?

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:11.167
Because you're sweating,
and the water hits you.

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:14.100
But when there's Gatorade,
it's sticky.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.100
-Sticky.
-And that's just nasty.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:17.567
-Yeah. You don't want sticky.
-That's just nasty,

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:19.834
but you tolerate it

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.901
because you ain't getting
Gatorade poured on you

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:24.234
unless you won.

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:27.234
I've never seen a loser
get Gatorade poured on them.

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.601
[Bell dings]
I've never seen that.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:29.634
-Here we go.

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:33.834
♪♪

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:35.200
-Oh.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.767
I'm sorry -- Look, hey.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:42.901
-Why you doing this?
-We got security by the door

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.634
in case something happens.

00:02:44.634 --> 00:02:47.501
Knicks or Lakers?
Holy moly.

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:50.434
What's happening?

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:51.934
-Believe it or not...

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.968
Believe it or not...

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:55.834
The Lakers are worse.

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:57.868
-Wow.
-Here's the reason why.

00:02:57.868 --> 00:02:59.033
-Yeah, tell us.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:03.067
-Are we really surprised
the Knicks lost?

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:05.267
Where's the suspense?
I mean, I'm disappointed.

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:08.200
-I see what you're saying.
-But most people expected...

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.734
-Yeah.
-At the very best,

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:15.734
a late first round exit --
at the most, second round,

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:17.601
you going home.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.501
You had LeBron.
-Okay.

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:22.601
-Anthony Davis.
Russell Westbrook.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:26.968
-Tinsel Town, purple and gold,
Hollywood, statues

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:30.434
of Shaq and Magic
and Kareem outside,

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:33.133
and Kobe and -- boy, I mean --

00:03:33.133 --> 00:03:39.200
And you are like 17, 18 games
under 500.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.300
You know, stealing money
from the public,

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.901
ain't thinking about
giving it back.

00:03:43.901 --> 00:03:46.501
I mean, look --
-The Knicks not --

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:49.234
-Look, look, look, look.

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:51.801
Give the Knicks credit
for this --

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:53.167
they've been honest.

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.868
[ Bell dings ]

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:57.968
♪♪

00:03:57.968 --> 00:03:59.501
Just saying.

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:02.267
[ Crowd gasps ]

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:03.801
-Tom Brady un-retiring.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:05.467
-You know what that's about,
right?

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:09.200
Y'all don't notice.
Allow me to help you out.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:10.734
My brother.

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:13.100
Tom Brady didn't un-retire.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.601
Giselle un-retired.

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:17.467
You think so?
-Oh, no, that brother --

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.968
that brother said
she sat up there in 2017.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:22.100
She told the world, "Y'all ain't
got to live with him

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.501
when this is over.
He comes home to me.

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:25.801
I love my man.

00:04:25.801 --> 00:04:27.901
Concussions, concussions,
and all of this other stuff.

00:04:27.901 --> 00:04:30.067
I want him heathy."
-Yeah.

00:04:30.067 --> 00:04:32.334
-Finally, couple of
Super Bowl titles later,

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:34.901
-Yeah.
-Actually, three to be exact,

00:04:34.901 --> 00:04:38.100
she sat up there and said,
"He said, 'Hey, it's time.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.334
I'm-a give it up.
I'm-a hang it up."

00:04:39.334 --> 00:04:41.000
-Done.
-Done.

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.601
Went home for two weeks.

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:45.100
[ Laughter, bell dings ]

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:48.734
And then said, "I think
I'm going to un-retire."

00:04:48.734 --> 00:04:50.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.467
That wasn't about Tom Brady.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:56.067
That was about the wife saying,
"I love you,

00:04:56.067 --> 00:05:00.934
but you -- I may have made
an error in my thinking.

00:05:00.934 --> 00:05:04.901
You might need
to go home, okay?"

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:08.167
Because listen, Tom Brady,
the brother's fly --

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:10.067
looks very good.
Looks like a GQ model.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:12.167
Rocks the Tom Ford blazers,
the whole bit.

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:14.734
Yeah, but, you know, we see him
when he out in public.

00:05:14.734 --> 00:05:16.133
-Yeah.
-We don't see him when he home

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:18.667
with T-shirts and shorts,
walking around the house.

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:21.501
And if you Giselle, you like,
"Wait, wait, wait a minute.

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:23.634
You sure you want to stay home?

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:25.400
Maybe I should support you
more."

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:29.467
"I should support you more
and you should go back to work."

00:05:29.467 --> 00:05:32.067
-That's right, go back to work.
-Go back to work, sweetheart,

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:35.334
and I'll see you
when you get home.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.400
That's what she did.
That was Giselle un-retiring.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.667
-Alright. I'll take that.
I like that.

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:39.934
-That's what that was about.

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:43.200
♪♪

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.200
-It's our last question.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:47.400
-Easily. Easily.
-The greatest of all time.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:48.734
-Easily.
-Wait, wait.

00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:51.434
You're saying easily.
-Yes, Michael Jordan.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:54.400
-Really?
-Easy. Easy. Easy.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:55.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:59.267
But you know what
the difficult part is?

00:05:59.267 --> 00:06:01.934
Is LeBron number two
or number three,

00:06:01.934 --> 00:06:04.767
to Kareem Abdul-Jabbar
being number two?

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:07.834
-Kareem Abdul-Jabbar.
-Sky high. Sky high.

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:10.534
-19-time All-Star,
six-time champion,

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:12.167
six-time league MVP,

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:14.934
all time leading scorer
in NBA history,

00:06:14.934 --> 00:06:17.267
and the only individual
in the history of the sport

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:19.667
with one unstoppable move
year after year after year

00:06:19.667 --> 00:06:22.167
spanning decades that no one
can still figure out.

00:06:22.167 --> 00:06:23.968
That's Kareem Abdul-Jabbar.
-Yeah.

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:26.767
-And won a title
for UCLA in college,

00:06:26.767 --> 00:06:30.534
and won a title at Powell
Memorial in New York City

00:06:30.534 --> 00:06:34.601
before he went to college.
LeBron James is phenomenal.

00:06:34.601 --> 00:06:36.734
He's on the Mount Rushmore
of basketball.

00:06:36.734 --> 00:06:39.567
He's all that and
a bag of chips.

00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:41.834
But he did lose six NBA finals.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:44.734
-Okay. Yeah.
-And he is the star on a team

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:46.634
that is presently
18 games --

00:06:46.634 --> 00:06:48.601
-Wait, wait. [ Laughs ]

00:06:48.601 --> 00:06:49.834
[ Bell dings ]

00:06:49.834 --> 00:06:51.901
That's it.
He settles it right there.

00:06:51.901 --> 00:06:57.367
Jordan and Kareem Abdul-Jabbar.
Stephen A. Smith, everybody.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:07:00.133
Watch him weekdays on ESPN,
"First Take,"

00:07:00.133 --> 00:07:02.534
And "Stephen A.'s World"
on ESPN Plus.

00:07:02.534 --> 00:07:04.801
That was fantastic.
Come back whenever you want.

